on.</article-title><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Freeman and Company</publisher-name><fpage>698</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Rieppel1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rieppel</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Reisz</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>The origin and early evolution of turtles,</article-title><source>Ann Rev Ecol Syst</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>22</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Meyer1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zardoya</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Recent advances in the (molecular) phylogeny of vertebrates,</article-title><source>Ann Rev Ecol Evol Syst</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>338</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Mller1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>M&#x000fc;ller</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Early loss and multiple return of the lower temporal arcade in diapsid reptiles,</article-title><source>Naturwissenschaften</source><volume>90</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>476</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14564408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Efremov1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Efremov</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1938</year><article-title>Some new Permian Reptiles of the USSR,</article-title><source>Dokl Akad Nauk SSSR</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>771</fpage><lpage>776</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Ivakhnenko1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ivakhnenko</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Permian Parareptiles of the USSR,</article-title><source>Trudy Paleont Inst Akad Nauk SSSR</source><volume>223</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>160</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Ivakhnenko2"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ivakhnenko</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>New Late Permian Nycteroleterids from Eastern Europe,</article-title><source>Paleont J</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>552</fpage><lpage>558</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Reisz2"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reisz</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Laurin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>The reptile <italic>Macroleter</italic>: First vertebrate evidence for correlation of Upper Permian continental strata of North America and Russia,</article-title><source>GSA Bulletin</source><volume>113</volume><fpage>1229</fpage><lpage>1233</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Tsuji1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsuji</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Cranial anatomy and phylogenetic affinities of the Permian parareptile <italic>Macroleter poezicus</italic>,</article-title><source>J Vert Paleont.</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>849</fpage><lpage>865</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Modesto1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Modesto</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Sues</surname><given-names>HD</given-names></name><name><surname>Damiani</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>A new Triassic procolophonoid reptile and its implications for procolophonoid survivorship during the Permo-Triassic extinction event,</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B.</source><volume>268</volume><fpage>2047</fpage><lpage>2052</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Norberg1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Norberg</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1978</year><article-title>Skull asymmetry, ear structure and function, and auditory localization in Tengmalta's Owl, <italic>Aegolius funereus</italic> (Linn.),</article-title><source>Phil Trans R Soc Lond</source><volume>282</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>410</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Wever1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wever</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name><name><surname>Werner</surname><given-names>YL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1970</year><article-title>The function of the middle ear in lizards: <italic>Crotaphytus collaris</italic> (lguanidae),</article-title><source>J Exp Zool</source><volume>175</volume><fpage>327</fpage><lpage>341 (1970)</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5478938</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Werner1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Werner</surname><given-names>YL</given-names></name><name><surname>Safford</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Seifan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Saunders</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Effects of age and size in the ears of gekkonomorph lizards: Middle-ear morphology with evolutionary implications,</article-title><source>Anat Rec</source><volume>283A</volume><fpage>212</fpage><lpage>223</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Wever2"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wever</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1978</year><article-title>The reptile ear: Its structure and function.</article-title><publisher-loc>Princeton</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Princeton University Press</publisher-name><fpage>1025</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Nummela1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nummela</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>S&#x000e1;nchez-Villagra</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Scaling of the marsupial middle ear and its functional significance,</article-title><source>J Zool</source><volume>270</volume><fpage>256</fpage><lpage>267</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Clack5"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clack</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>The evolution of tetrapod ears and the fossil record,</article-title><source>Brain Behav Evol</source><volume>50</volume><fpage>198</fpage><lpage>212</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9310195</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000889-Manley1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Manley</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1972</year><article-title>The middle ear of the tokay gecko,</article-title><source>J Comp Physiol</source><volume>81</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>250</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.000088